  "commits_data": [
    {
      "id": "bd9ceaebef86a30f5f45a8887fd01883dd0d1993",
      "short_id": "bd9ceaeb",
      "created_at": "2021-06-16T07:12:12.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "4fdf3f10389c28918128e34c0eeeda5a435617b7"
      ],
      "title": "wslua: a tvbuff doesn't have an \"actual length\".",
      "message": "wslua: a tvbuff doesn't have an \"actual length\".\n\nIt has a \"reported length\", which is the closes thing to an \"actual\nlength\", as it represents the length the packet, or subset thereof, had\non the network, and a \"captured length\", which is the amount of the\npacket that the capture process saved.\n\nIn 99.999999999999999999999999999999% of all cases, a dissector should\nlook at the \"reported length\", not at the \"captured length\".\n\nRename the \"len\" method to \"captured_len\", leaving \"len\" around for\nbackwards compatibility.\n\nFix the documentation to reflect reality, to avoid issues such as #15655.\n",
      "author_name": "Guy Harris",
      "author_email": "gharris@sonic.net",
      "authored_date": "2021-06-15T23:24:01.000-07:00",
      "committer_name": "Wireshark GitLab Utility",
      "committer_email": "gerald+gitlab-utility@wireshark.org",
      "committed_date": "2021-06-16T07:12:12.000+00:00",
